llama.cpp (as fetched by Ollama v0.35.1, llama.cpp b11232): a gfx803 kernel
for token generation with a q8_0 KV cache and grouped-query attention.

WHY
---
On gfx803, token generation with a q8_0 KV cache slows down as the context
grows, much more than the extra K/V traffic explains. Qwen3 8B Q4_K_M on an
RX 590, llama-bench tg64: 27.9 tok/s on an empty context, 23.7 tok/s 4096
tokens deep, 20.9 tok/s 8192 deep. With an f16 KV cache, twice the bytes, it
runs 24.0 tok/s 8192 deep.

Generation (one query token) with a quantized KV cache runs the vec kernel
(fattn-vec.cuh). On gfx803 its q8_0 instance needs 229 VGPRs, so a SIMD holds
one of its waves and nothing hides the latency of its K/V loads. At 8192
tokens one layer of Qwen3 takes 286 us (test-backend-ops perf, 8 K/V heads x
4 query heads, head size 128), which moves K/V at about 60 GB/s of the card's
256 GB/s. Time follows the number of query heads, not the bytes: Qwen2.5-
Coder's shape (4 K/V heads x 7 query heads, half the K/V bytes) takes 280 us.
The vec kernel reads each K/V head once per query head of its group.

The vec kernel does not fit gfx803 with less: capping it at 128 VGPRs spills
157 VGPRs and runs 6x slower. Letting each block serve the 4 query heads of
a group (sharing every K/V load) spills too, 26 VGPRs at 4 heads and 85 at 8,
and runs slower than the original.

WHAT
----
fattn-gcn4-decode.cuh adds flash_attn_gcn4_decode_q8_0<D, ncols2>, built so
that few registers stay live:

  - A block serves ncols2 (2, 4 or 8) query heads that share one K/V head,
    so each K/V row is read once for all of them. A group whose size is not
    a multiple of ncols2 (Qwen2.5's 7) ends in a partial tile.
  - Scores: every lane owns one K row and dots it with all ncols2 query
    vectors. The query vectors sit in shared memory, where every lane reads
    the same address. A pair of q8_0 blocks is 68 bytes, so with 4-byte
    aligned rows each pair loads as 17 whole dwords.
  - Weighted sum over V: every lane owns D/64 output dimensions, so a warp
    reads each V row in one coalesced sweep. The softmax weights travel from
    the lane that computed them by readlane.
  - The four warps of a block each take 64 rows of a 256-row slice and are
    combined in shared memory at the end; blocks split the KV length and
    are combined by launch_fattn's usual flash_attn_combine_results.

The D=128 kernels use 66 / 86 / 104 VGPRs at ncols2 = 2 / 4 / 8, with no
spills. Wider groups read K/V fewer times but give fewer, longer blocks, so
the host picks ncols2 = 8 from 128 blocks, 4 from 32 blocks, else 2 (block
counts measured on the RX 590, 36 CUs). Per layer, test-backend-ops perf:

    K/V length            256    1024    4096    8192
    Qwen3 shape, vec      27.2   57.6    169     287 us
    Qwen3 shape, new      22.9   40.0    92.6    148 us
    Qwen2.5 shape, vec    27.3   58.7    139     280 us
    Qwen2.5 shape, new    22.9   37.1    77.1    137 us

ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext() tries the new kernel first wherever the kernel
selection picks the vec kernel. It applies only on gfx803 (cc ==
GGML_CUDA_CC_GCN4) for one query token, q8_0 K and V of head size 64, 128 or
256, GQA ratio 2 or more, a mask, no ALiBi and no logit softcap, a KV length
that is a multiple of 256, and dword-aligned K rows; everything else goes to
the vec kernel as before. Its device code is compiled for GCN4 only.

Result on an RX 590, llama-bench, flash attention on, q8_0 KV cache, tg64 at
depth 0 / 4096 / 8192 tokens:

    Qwen3 8B Q4_K_M           27.9 / 23.7 / 20.9  ->  28.1 / 26.0 / 24.4 tok/s
    Qwen2.5-Coder 7B Q4_K_M   30.1 / 27.1 / 24.8  ->  30.3 / 28.8 / 27.2 tok/s

Prompt processing is unchanged.

Verified on an RX 590: test-backend-ops test -b ROCm0 -o FLASH_ATTN_EXT
passes against the CPU backend for q8_0 (364 stock cases), q4_0 and f16 K/V,
plus 120 added grouped-query decode cases per type: head sizes 64, 128 and
256, GQA ratios 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 12 and 16, 4 K/V heads, KV length 512 and
1024, with and without sinks, and 2 K/V heads x 3 sequences. Through Ollama
(q8_0 KV cache, a 5.2k-token prompt, greedy, 128 tokens), the logprobs of
the tokens before the first near-tie stay within 0.04 (Qwen3 8B) and 0.05
(Qwen2.5-Coder 7B) of a CPU run, as with the vec kernel (0.04, 0.03), and
generation runs 22.3 -> 24.4 tok/s (Qwen3) and 25.6 -> 27.3 tok/s
(Qwen2.5-Coder). To reproduce,
build llama.cpp b11232 with GGML_HIP=ON and AMDGPU_TARGETS=gfx803, then run
with and without the patch:

    llama-bench -m <Qwen3 8B Q4_K_M> -ngl 99 -fa 1 -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0 \
        -p 0 -n 64 -d 0,4096,8192

Applies on its own; it does not touch the files of 100- and 101-.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn-gcn4-decode.cuh b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn-gcn4-decode.cuh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..12c2b01
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn-gcn4-decode.cuh
@@ -0,0 +1,336 @@
+#include "common.cuh"
+#include "fattn-common.cuh"
+
+// Token generation with a q8_0 KV cache on gfx803 (GCN4).
+//
+// The generic vec kernel needs about 229 VGPRs here, so a SIMD holds one of its waves and
+// nothing hides the latency of its K/V loads: at 8192 tokens of context it moves K/V at about
+// a quarter of the card's bandwidth. Narrowing its register budget spills, and widening it to
+// serve several query heads per K/V row (grouped-query attention) spills too.
+//
+// This kernel reorganizes the work so that few registers are live. A block serves ncols2
+// query heads that share one K/V head, so each K/V row is read once for all of them. For the
+// scores, every lane owns one K row and dots it with all ncols2 query vectors, which sit in
+// shared memory where every lane reads the same address. For the weighted sum over V, every
+// lane owns D/64 output dimensions, so a warp reads each V row in one coalesced sweep, and
+// the softmax weights travel from the lane that computed them by readlane.
+
+// GCN runs 64-wide wavefronts. The host pass sees WARP_SIZE as 32, so the launch needs this too.
+static constexpr int fattn_gcn4_warp_size = 64;
+static constexpr int fattn_gcn4_nwarps    = 4;
+static constexpr int fattn_gcn4_rows      = fattn_gcn4_nwarps*fattn_gcn4_warp_size; // K/V rows per block iteration
+
+static_assert(fattn_gcn4_rows == FATTN_KQ_STRIDE, "the KV length must be a multiple of the rows per iteration");
+
+template <int D, int ncols2> // D == head size, ncols2 == query heads per block
+__launch_bounds__(fattn_gcn4_nwarps*fattn_gcn4_warp_size, 1)
+static __global__ void flash_attn_gcn4_decode_q8_0(
+        const char * Q_ptr,
+        const char * K_ptr,
+        const char * V_ptr,
+        const char * mask_ptr,
+        const char * sinks_ptr,
+        const int  * KV_max_ptr,
+        float      * dst_ptr,
+        float2     * dst_meta_ptr,
+        const float scale,
+        const float max_bias,
+        const float m0,
+        const float m1,
+        const uint32_t n_head_log2,
+        const float logit_softcap,
+        const int32_t ne00, const uint3   ne01, const int32_t ne02, const int32_t ne03,
+                            const int32_t nb01, const int32_t nb02, const int32_t nb03,
+        const int32_t ne10, const int32_t ne11, const int32_t ne12, const int32_t ne13,
+                            const int32_t nb11, const int32_t nb12, const int64_t nb13,
+                            const int32_t nb21, const int32_t nb22, const int64_t nb23,
+                            const int32_t ne31, const int32_t ne32, const int32_t ne33,
+                            const int32_t nb31, const int32_t nb32, const int64_t nb33) {
+    ggml_cuda_pdl_lc();
+#if defined(FLASH_ATTN_AVAILABLE) && defined(GCN4)
+    constexpr int nblocks_row = D/QK8_0;                // q8_0 blocks per K/V row
+    constexpr int dims_lane   = D/fattn_gcn4_warp_size; // output dimensions per lane
+    static_assert(nblocks_row % 2 == 0, "K rows are read in pairs of q8_0 blocks");
+
+    const int lane = threadIdx.x;
+    const int warp = threadIdx.y;
+
+    // A group whose size is not a multiple of ncols2 ends in a partial tile.
+    const int gqa_ratio    = ne02 / ne12;
+    const int ntiles_z_gqa = (gqa_ratio + ncols2 - 1) / ncols2;
+    const int sequence     = blockIdx.z / (ntiles_z_gqa*ne12);
+    const int zt           = blockIdx.z - sequence*(ntiles_z_gqa*ne12);
+    const int head_KV      = zt / ntiles_z_gqa;
+    const int head0        = head_KV*gqa_ratio + (zt - head_KV*ntiles_z_gqa)*ncols2;
+    const int nheads       = min(ncols2, (head_KV + 1)*gqa_ratio - head0);
+
+    const char * K     = K_ptr + nb13*sequence + int64_t(nb12)*head_KV;
+    const char * V     = V_ptr + nb23*sequence + int64_t(nb22)*head_KV;
+    const half * maskh = (const half *) (mask_ptr + nb33*(sequence % ne33));
+
+    __shared__ float Q_s[ncols2][D];
+    __shared__ float KQ_max_s[fattn_gcn4_nwarps][ncols2];
+    __shared__ float VKQ_s[ncols2][D];
+    __shared__ float KQ_sum_s[ncols2];
+
+    ggml_cuda_pdl_sync();
+    for (int i = warp*fattn_gcn4_warp_size + lane; i < ncols2*D; i += fattn_gcn4_rows) {
+        const int c = i / D;
+        const float * Q_c = (const float *) (Q_ptr + nb03*sequence + int64_t(nb02)*(head0 + c));
+        Q_s[c][i % D] = c < nheads ? scale*Q_c[i % D] : 0.0f;
+    }
+    __syncthreads();
+
+    float KQ_max[ncols2];
+    float KQ_sum[ncols2]; // this lane's share, reduced over the warp at the end
+    float VKQ[ncols2][dims_lane];
+#pragma unroll
+    for (int c = 0; c < ncols2; ++c) {
+        KQ_max[c] = -FLT_MAX/2.0f;
+        KQ_sum[c] = 0.0f;
+#pragma unroll
+        for (int e = 0; e < dims_lane; ++e) {
+            VKQ[c][e] = 0.0f;
+        }
+    }
+
+    // Each lane's V dimensions lie in one q8_0 block of the row.
+    const int dim0   = lane*dims_lane;
+    const int ib_V   = dim0 / QK8_0;
+    const int iqs_V  = dim0 % QK8_0;
+
+    const int k_VKQ_max = KV_max_ptr ? KV_max_ptr[sequence*gridDim.x + blockIdx.x] : ne11;
+    for (int k0 = blockIdx.y*fattn_gcn4_rows + warp*fattn_gcn4_warp_size; k0 < k_VKQ_max; k0 += gridDim.y*fattn_gcn4_rows) {
+        const int k = k0 + lane;
+
+        // Q_s does not change inside this loop, so the compiler would otherwise hoist all
+        // ncols2*D of its values into registers; an offset it cannot see through keeps them
+        // as shared memory reads.
+        int Q_off = 0;
+        asm volatile("" : "+s"(Q_off));
+        const float * Q_it = &Q_s[0][0] + Q_off;
+
+        float KQ[ncols2];
+#pragma unroll
+        for (int c = 0; c < ncols2; ++c) {
+            KQ[c] = 0.0f;
+        }
+
+        // A pair of q8_0 blocks is 68 bytes, so with 4-byte aligned rows each pair starts
+        // 4-byte aligned and loads as 17 whole dwords: the first block's scale is the low
+        // half of dword 0 and its quants start at byte 2, the second block's scale is the
+        // high half of dword 8 and its quants are dwords 9-16.
+        const int * K_row = (const int *) (K + int64_t(k)*nb11);
+#pragma unroll
+        for (int ib = 0; ib < nblocks_row; ib += 2) {
+            int w[17];
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int l = 0; l < 17; ++l) {
+                w[l] = K_row[(ib/2)*17 + l];
+            }
+            const float d0 = __half2float(__ushort_as_half(uint16_t(w[0] & 0xFFFF)));
+            const float d1 = __half2float(__ushort_as_half(uint16_t(uint32_t(w[8]) >> 16)));
+
+            float sum0[ncols2];
+            float sum1[ncols2];
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int c = 0; c < ncols2; ++c) {
+                sum0[c] = 0.0f;
+                sum1[c] = 0.0f;
+            }
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int b = 0; b < QK8_0; ++b) {
+                const float k0f = float(int8_t(w[(b + 2)/4] >> (8*((b + 2) % 4))));
+                const float k1f = float(int8_t(w[9 + b/4]   >> (8*(b % 4))));
+#pragma unroll
+                for (int c = 0; c < ncols2; ++c) {
+                    sum0[c] += k0f*Q_it[c*D +  ib     *QK8_0 + b];
+                    sum1[c] += k1f*Q_it[c*D + (ib + 1)*QK8_0 + b];
+                }
+            }
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int c = 0; c < ncols2; ++c) {
+                KQ[c] += d0*sum0[c] + d1*sum1[c];
+            }
+        }
+
+        const float mask_k = __half2float(maskh[k]);
+#pragma unroll
+        for (int c = 0; c < ncols2; ++c) {
+            KQ[c] += mask_k;
+            const float KQ_max_new   = fmaxf(KQ_max[c], warp_reduce_max<fattn_gcn4_warp_size>(KQ[c]));
+            const float KQ_max_scale = expf(KQ_max[c] - KQ_max_new);
+            KQ_max[c] = KQ_max_new;
+            KQ[c]     = expf(KQ[c] - KQ_max_new);
+            KQ_sum[c] = KQ_sum[c]*KQ_max_scale + KQ[c];
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int e = 0; e < dims_lane; ++e) {
+                VKQ[c][e] *= KQ_max_scale;
+            }
+        }
+
+#pragma unroll 4
+        for (int r = 0; r < fattn_gcn4_warp_size; ++r) {
+            const block_q8_0 * V_r = (const block_q8_0 *) (V + int64_t(k0 + r)*nb21) + ib_V;
+            const float d = __half2float(V_r->d);
+            int8_t qs[dims_lane];
+            if constexpr (dims_lane == 1) {
+                qs[0] = V_r->qs[iqs_V];
+            } else {
+                ggml_cuda_memcpy_1<dims_lane, 2>(qs, V_r->qs + iqs_V);
+            }
+            float v[dims_lane];
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int e = 0; e < dims_lane; ++e) {
+                v[e] = d*float(qs[e]);
+            }
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int c = 0; c < ncols2; ++c) {
+                const float p = __int_as_float(__builtin_amdgcn_readlane(__float_as_int(KQ[c]), r));
+#pragma unroll
+                for (int e = 0; e < dims_lane; ++e) {
+                    VKQ[c][e] += p*v[e];
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    // Combine the warps: rescale each to the block's maximum, then sum them in shared memory.
+    if (lane == 0) {
+#pragma unroll
+        for (int c = 0; c < ncols2; ++c) {
+            KQ_max_s[warp][c] = KQ_max[c];
+        }
+    }
+    __syncthreads();
+#pragma unroll
+    for (int c = 0; c < ncols2; ++c) {
+        float KQ_max_block = KQ_max_s[0][c];
+#pragma unroll
+        for (int w = 1; w < fattn_gcn4_nwarps; ++w) {
+            KQ_max_block = fmaxf(KQ_max_block, KQ_max_s[w][c]);
+        }
+        const float KQ_max_scale = expf(KQ_max[c] - KQ_max_block);
+        KQ_max[c] = KQ_max_block;
+        KQ_sum[c] = warp_reduce_sum<fattn_gcn4_warp_size>(KQ_sum[c])*KQ_max_scale;
+#pragma unroll
+        for (int e = 0; e < dims_lane; ++e) {
+            VKQ[c][e] *= KQ_max_scale;
+        }
+    }
+#pragma unroll
+    for (int w = 0; w < fattn_gcn4_nwarps; ++w) {
+        if (warp == w) {
+#pragma unroll
+            for (int c = 0; c < ncols2; ++c) {
+#pragma unroll
+                for (int e = 0; e < dims_lane; ++e) {
+                    VKQ_s[c][dim0 + e] = w == 0 ? VKQ[c][e] : VKQ_s[c][dim0 + e] + VKQ[c][e];
+                }
+                if (lane == 0) {
+                    KQ_sum_s[c] = w == 0 ? KQ_sum[c] : KQ_sum_s[c] + KQ_sum[c];
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        __syncthreads();
+    }
+
+    for (int i = warp*fattn_gcn4_warp_size + lane; i < ncols2*D; i += fattn_gcn4_rows) {
+        const int c = i / D;
+        if (c >= nheads) {
+            break;
+        }
+        float KQ_max_c = KQ_max_s[0][c];
+#pragma unroll
+        for (int w = 1; w < fattn_gcn4_nwarps; ++w) {
+            KQ_max_c = fmaxf(KQ_max_c, KQ_max_s[w][c]);
+        }
+        float KQ_sum_c = KQ_sum_s[c];
+        float val      = VKQ_s[c][i % D];
+        if (sinks_ptr && blockIdx.y == 0) {
+            const float sink        = ((const float *) sinks_ptr)[head0 + c];
+            const float KQ_max_new  = fmaxf(KQ_max_c, sink);
+            const float KQ_max_scale = expf(KQ_max_c - KQ_max_new);
+            KQ_max_c = KQ_max_new;
+            KQ_sum_c = KQ_sum_c*KQ_max_scale + expf(sink - KQ_max_new);
+            val     *= KQ_max_scale;
+        }
+        const int j_dst = (sequence*int(ne01.z)*ne02 + head0 + c)*gridDim.y + blockIdx.y;
+        dst_ptr[j_dst*D + i % D] = gridDim.y == 1 ? val/KQ_sum_c : val;
+        if (gridDim.y != 1 && i % D == 0) {
+            dst_meta_ptr[j_dst] = make_float2(KQ_max_c, KQ_sum_c);
+        }
+    }
+#else
+    GGML_UNUSED_VARS(Q_ptr, K_ptr, V_ptr, mask_ptr, sinks_ptr, KV_max_ptr, dst_ptr, dst_meta_ptr, scale,
+        max_bias, m0, m1, n_head_log2, logit_softcap,
+        ne00, ne01, ne02, ne03,
+              nb01, nb02, nb03,
+        ne10, ne11, ne12, ne13,
+              nb11, nb12, nb13,
+              nb21, nb22, nb23,
+              ne31, ne32, ne33,
+              nb31, nb32, nb33);
+    NO_DEVICE_CODE;
+#endif // defined(FLASH_ATTN_AVAILABLE) && defined(GCN4)
+}
+
+template <int D, int ncols2>
+static void ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_gcn4_decode_case(ggml_backend_cuda_context & ctx, ggml_tensor * dst) {
+    launch_fattn<D, 1, ncols2>(ctx, dst, flash_attn_gcn4_decode_q8_0<D, ncols2>, fattn_gcn4_nwarps, 0,
+        fattn_gcn4_rows, false, false, false, false, fattn_gcn4_warp_size);
+}
+
+template <int D>
+static void ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_gcn4_decode_switch_ncols2(ggml_backend_cuda_context & ctx, ggml_tensor * dst, const int gqa_ratio) {
+    // Wider head groups read K/V fewer times but give fewer, longer blocks, which only pays
+    // off once there are enough blocks to fill the GPU. The block counts at which a width
+    // starts to win were measured on an RX 590 (36 CUs) with 4 and 8 K/V heads.
+    const ggml_tensor * K = dst->src[1];
+    auto nblocks = [&](const int ncols2) {
+        return K->ne[2]*K->ne[3]*((gqa_ratio + ncols2 - 1)/ncols2)*(K->ne[1]/fattn_gcn4_rows);
+    };
+    if (gqa_ratio > 4 && nblocks(8) >= 128) {
+        ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_gcn4_decode_case<D, 8>(ctx, dst);
+    } else if (gqa_ratio > 2 && nblocks(4) >= 32) {
+        ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_gcn4_decode_case<D, 4>(ctx, dst);
+    } else {
+        ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_gcn4_decode_case<D, 2>(ctx, dst);
+    }
+}
+
+// Runs the kernel above and returns true if it applies to dst, else returns false.
+static bool ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_gcn4_decode(ggml_backend_cuda_context & ctx, ggml_tensor * dst) {
+    const ggml_tensor * Q    = dst->src[0];
+    const ggml_tensor * K    = dst->src[1];
+    const ggml_tensor * V    = dst->src[2];
+    const ggml_tensor * mask = dst->src[3];
+
+    if (ggml_cuda_info().devices[ggml_cuda_get_device()].cc != GGML_CUDA_CC_GCN4) {
+        return false;
+    }
+
+    float max_bias;
+    float logit_softcap;
+    memcpy(&max_bias,      (const float *) dst->op_params + 1, sizeof(float));
+    memcpy(&logit_softcap, (const float *) dst->op_params + 2, sizeof(float));
+
+    const int gqa_ratio = Q->ne[2] / K->ne[2];
+    if (Q->ne[1] != 1 || gqa_ratio < 2 || !mask || max_bias != 0.0f || logit_softcap != 0.0f) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    if (K->type != GGML_TYPE_Q8_0 || V->type != GGML_TYPE_Q8_0 || K->ne[0] != V->ne[0] || K->ne[1] % fattn_gcn4_rows != 0) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    // K rows are read as whole dwords.
+    if (uintptr_t(K->data) % 4 != 0 || K->nb[1] % 4 != 0 || K->nb[2] % 4 != 0 || K->nb[3] % 4 != 0) {
+        return false;
+    }
+
+    switch (K->ne[0]) {
+        case  64: ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_gcn4_decode_switch_ncols2< 64>(ctx, dst, gqa_ratio); return true;
+        case 128: ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_gcn4_decode_switch_ncols2<128>(ctx, dst, gqa_ratio); return true;
+        case 256: ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_gcn4_decode_switch_ncols2<256>(ctx, dst, gqa_ratio); return true;
+        default:  return false;
+    }
+}
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn.cu
index ad4d1df..9b2ef40 100644
